[42.588304, "o", "    lines = ['# Multiverse analysis report', '', 'The analysis constructs the selected binary skin-tone predictor, selected any-event outcome, and a dyad-level binomial logistic model for every universe. Binary predictors are standardized by their sample standard deviation; estimates and standard errors are reported on that comparable standardized scale.', '', f'- Universes processed: {len(records)}', f'- Successful fits: {len(good)}', f'- Failed fits: {len(records)-len(good)}']\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[42.588692, "o", "    if len(vals): lines += [f'- Standardized estimate range: {vals.min():.4f} to {vals.max():.4f}', f'- Median standardized estimate: {np.median(vals):.4f}', f'- Positive estimates: {int((vals>0).sum())}; negative estimates: {int((vals<0).sum())}']\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[42.589597, "o", "    lines += ['', '## Decision implementation', '- `mean_raters`, `rater1_only`, and `both_raters_thresholded` define the dark indicator before applying the selected threshold.', '- Outcomes are either straight red cards or either type of sending-off.', '- Games are ignored, used as frequency weights, or entered as log(games).', '- Covariate options add league, position, height, weight, and optionally referee-country and bias variables.', '- Inference uses iid, player-clustered, two-way player/referee-clustered, or the crossed-group robust path selected by the universe.']\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[42.590123, "o", "    lines += ['', '## Interpretation of spread', 'The JSONL contains the complete numerical specification curve without a verdict. The spread reflects changes in outcome definition, skin-tone construction and threshold, exposure treatment, adjustment set, and dependence inference. Estimates and confidence intervals should be compared using the standardized fields.']\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[42.59026, "o", "    open('/app/results.md','w').write('\\n'.join(lines)+'\\n')\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
