[455.279358, "o", "printf '\\nReport:\\n'; cat /app/results.md\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\r\nReport:\r\n"]
[455.279894, "o", "# Multiverse analysis report\r\n\r\nThe selections-driven analysis constructs the selected skin-tone indicator and any-event outcome, then fits a dyad-level binomial logistic model for every universe. The focal binary predictor is standardized by its sample SD, and estimates, standard errors, and intervals are reported on that comparable scale.\r\n\r\n- Universes processed: 256\r\n- Successful fits: 66\r\n- Failed fits: 190\r\n- Standardized estimate range: -0.0258 to 0.0645\r\n- Median standardized estimate: 0.0348\r\n- Positive estimates: 61; negative estimates: 5\r\n\r\n## Decision implementation\r\n- Skin tone uses the selected rater combination and threshold.\r\n- The outcome is straight red cards or either sending-off type.\r\n- Games are ignored, used as frequency weights, or adjusted with log(games).\r\n- Covariate sets add league, position, height, weight, and optionally referee-country and bias variables.\r\n- Inference uses the selected iid, player-clustered, two-way clustered, or crossed-group robust path.\r\n\r\n## Interpretation\r\nThe JSONL contains one record per universe and no verdict; the standardized fields are the comparable specification-curve estimands.\r\n"]
[455.279971, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@e68efb9ca62c:/app# "]
[465.96578, "i", "python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json, collections\nrows=[json.loads(x) for x in open('/app/universes.jsonl')]\nprint('failure notes:')\nfor note,n in collections.Counter(r.get('notes','') for r in rows if not r['converged']).most_common(10): print(n, note)\nprint('\\nfailures by decisions:')\nfor key in ['covariate_adjustment','dependence_inference','games_exposure_handling']:\n c=collections.defaultdict(lambda:[0,0])\n for r in rows:\n  c[r['decisions'][key]][r['converged']==True]+=1\n print(key,dict(c))\nPY\n"]
[465.966426, "o", "python3 - <<'PY'\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> import json, collections\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> rows=[json.loads(x) for x in open('/app/universes.jsonl')]\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> print('failure notes:')\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[465.966673, "o", "for note,n in collections.Counter(r.get('notes','') for r in rows if not r['converged']).most_common(10): print(n, note)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> print('\\nfailures by decisions:')\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[465.96681, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> for key in ['covariate_adjustment','dependence_inference','games_exposure_handling']:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
