[1827.228402, "o", "# Multiverse analysis report\r\n\r\nThe selections-driven analysis constructs the selected skin-tone indicator and any-event outcome, then fits a dyad-level binomial logistic model for every universe. The focal binary predictor is standardized by its sample SD, and estimates, standard errors, and intervals are reported on that comparable scale.\r\n\r\n- Universes processed: 256\r\n- Successful fits: 93\r\n- Failed fits: 163\r\n- Standardized estimate range: -0.0258 to 0.0645\r\n- Median standardized estimate: 0.0286\r\n- Positive estimates: 88; negative estimates: 5\r\n\r\n## Decision implementation\r\n- Skin tone uses the selected rater combination and threshold.\r\n- The outcome is straight red cards or either sending-off type.\r\n- Games are ignored, used as frequency weights, or adjusted with log(games).\r\n- Covariate sets add league, position, height, weight, and optionally referee-country and bias variables.\r\n- Inference uses the selected iid, player-clustered, two-way clustered, or crossed-group robust path.\r\n\r\n## Interpretation\r\nThe JSONL contains one record per universe and no verdict; the standardized fields are the comparable specification-curve estimands.\r\n"]
[1827.228569, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@e68efb9ca62c:/app# "]
[1839.179214, "i", "python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json, collections\np='/app/universes.jsonl'\nrows=[json.loads(x) for x in open(p)]\ngood=[r for r in rows if r.get('converged') is True and r.get('estimate_standardized') is not None]\ndecisions=sorted(good[0]['decisions']) if good else []\nlines=['','## Decision-level movement','Among successful fits, the following ranges show how much the standardized estimate varied within each option; larger ranges indicate decisions associated with more movement in the specification curve.']\nsummary=[]\nfor d in decisions:\n    by=collections.defaultdict(list)\n    for r in good: by[r['decisions'][d]].append(r['estimate_standardized'])\n    ranges=[]\n    for opt, vals in by.items():\n        ranges.append((opt,min(vals),max(vals),max(vals)-min(vals),len(vals)))\n    if ranges:\n        overall=max(x[3] for x in ranges)\n        summary.append((overall,d,ranges))\nfor overall,d,ranges in sorted(summary,reverse=True):\n    text='; '.join(f'`{o}`: {lo:.4f} to {hi:.4f} (n={n})' for o,lo,hi,_,n in sorted(ranges))\n    lines.append(f'- **{d}** (largest within-option range {overall:.4f}): {text}')\nwith open('/app/results.md','a') as f: f.write('\\n'.join(lines)+'\\n')\nprint('\\n'.join(lines))\nPY\npython3 -m py_compile /app/analysis.py\npython3 - <<'PY'\nimport json,glob,os\nrows=[json.loads(x) for x in open('/app/universes.jsonl')]\nassert len(rows)==256 and len({r['universe_id'] for r in rows})==256\nassert len(glob.glob('/app/universes/*.yaml'))==256\nassert all('decisions' in r and 'estimate_standardized' in r and 'converged' in r for r in rows)\nprint('FINAL VALIDATION OK:',len(rows),'records;',sum(r['converged'] for r in rows),'converged')\nPY\n"]
[1839.17945, "o", "python3 - <<'PY'\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1839.179691, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> import json, collections\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> p='/app/universes.jsonl'\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1839.182026, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> rows=[json.loads(x) for x in open(p)]\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> good=[r for r in rows if r.get('converged') is True and r.get('estimate_standardized') is not None]\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> decisions=sorted(good[0]['decisions']) if good else []\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> lines=['','## Decision-level movement','Among successful fits, the following ranges show how much the standardized estimate varied within each option; larger ranges indicate decisions associated with more movement in the specification curve.']\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> summary=[]\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> for d in decisions:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>     by=collections.defaultdict(list)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>     for r in good: by[r['decisions'][d]].append(r['estimate_standardized'])\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>     ranges=[]\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>     for opt, vals in by.items():\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>         ranges.append((opt,min(vals),max(vals),max(vals)-min(vals),len(vals)))\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>     if ranges:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>         overall=max(x[3] for x in ranges)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>         summary.append((overall,d,ranges))\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> for overall,d,ranges in sorted(summary,reverse=True):\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>     text='; '.join(f'`{o}`: {lo:.4f} to {hi:.4f} (n={n})' for o,lo,hi,_,n in sorted(ranges))\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>     lines.append(f'- **{d}** (largest within-option range {overall:.4f}): {text}')\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> with open('/app/results.md','a') as f: f.write('\\n'.join(lines)+'\\n')\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> print('\\n'.join(lines))\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> PY\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1839.19956, "o", "\r\n## Decision-level movement\r\nAmong successful fits, the following ranges show how much the standardized estimate varied within each option; larger ranges indicate decisions associated with more movement in the specification curve.\r\n- **skin_tone_threshold** (largest within-option range 0.0903): `above_050`: -0.0145 to 0.0622 (n=30); `at_least_050`: -0.0258 to 0.0645 (n=38); `at_least_075`: 0.0076 to 0.0622 (n=25)\r\n- **dependence_inference** (largest within-option range 0.0903): `model_based_iid`: -0.0258 to 0.0645 (n=72); `player_clustered`: 0.0055 to 0.0624 (n=7); `random_intercepts`: 0.0055 to 0.0624 (n=7); `two_way_clustered`: 0.0055 to 0.0624 (n=7)\r\n- **covariate_adjustment** (largest within-option range 0.0903): `player_and_league_covariates`: 0.0034 to 0.0624 (n=27); `skin_tone_only`: -0.0258 to 0.0645 (n=66)\r\n- **skin_tone_rater_combination** (largest within-option range 0.0880): `both_raters_thresholded`: -0.0258 to 0.0622 (n=32); `mean_raters`: -0.0258 to 0.0622 (n=37); `rater1_only`: -0.0136 to 0.0645 (n=24)\r\n- **red_card_outcome_definition** (largest within-option range 0.0697): `any_sending_off`: -0.0258 to 0.0439 (n=42); `straight_red_only`: -0.0026 to 0.0645 (n=51)\r\n- **games_exposure_handling** (largest within-option range 0.0545): `adjust_for_log_games`: 0.0284 to 0.0645 (n=28); `games_frequency_weight`: -0.0258 to 0.0287 (n=27); `unweighted_dyads`: 0.0034 to 0.0502 (n=38)\r\n"]
